{
  // Bridges (docs/design.md, "Bridges"; the owner, 2026-10-24: destructible, can be repaired, never built by players, no weight
  // limit; every piece stands alone). The map places them over water (its "bridges" list), the sandbox too; they are neutral for
  // good (nobody's, nobody targets one on his own) and block nothing. The footprint's long side (h) is the road: every footprint
  // cell carries the bridge's road kind, its cells over water are the deck (flat ground while the span stands). Sizes fixed with
  // the art (1 cell = 2 m): the stone arch 3 x 8 (6 x 16 m, one lane: a village lane, paved), the concrete beam 5 x 12 (10 x 24 m,
  // two lanes, paved), the metal truss 9 x 18 (18 x 36 m, four lanes, highway). Heights to the parapet or truss top (tenths of a
  // metre). Building armour; HP stone 2,500, concrete 3,500, metal 4,500.
  // Stages (bridge.stages): 0 above 70% HP, 1 above 40%, 2 (heavy, still passable) down to 0 HP; at 0 HP the span falls (stage 3:
  // the deck is lifted, whoever is on it goes into the water) and the ruin stays at 1 HP. Repair: builders (workers, the bulldozer)
  // on a Repair order, either side's; one builder restores the whole bar in repairable.fullPercentOfBuild percent of buildTime
  // (never built: buildTime is only the repair's measure), the 2nd adds half, a 3rd nothing (bridge.helpers); a fallen span's
  // deck is laid again at bridge.reopen percent of max HP (one worker from a fall: stone 12 s, concrete 18 s, metal 24 s).
